[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 3. V&V organization

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SVVP-003-MILUAV
TITLE: V&V Organization
STATEMENT: V&V organization includes V&V manager, V&V engineers, independent verification team, and validation specialists with defined roles and responsibilities.
RATIONALE: V&V organization ensures effective verification and validation.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SVVP-004-MILUAV
TITLE: V&V Independence
STATEMENT: V&V activities shall be independent of development activities with separate reporting structure and authority for military software development.
RATIONALE: V&V independence ensures objective assessment.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SVVP-005-MILUAV
TITLE: V&V Authority
STATEMENT: V&V shall have authority to approve or reject software releases based on verification and validation results for military systems.
RATIONALE: V&V authority ensures quality standards enforcement.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 4. Verification activities

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SVVP-006-MILUAV
TITLE: Requirements Verification
STATEMENT: Requirements verification includes completeness, consistency, traceability, and testability verification for all software requirements.
RATIONALE: Requirements verification ensures requirement quality.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SVVP-007-MILUAV
TITLE: Design Verification
STATEMENT: Design verification includes architecture verification, interface verification, and design compliance verification for military software.
RATIONALE: Design verification ensures design quality and compliance.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SVVP-008-MILUAV
TITLE: Code Verification
STATEMENT: Code verification includes static analysis, code reviews, and coding standards compliance verification for military software.
RATIONALE: Code verification ensures code quality and security.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SVVP-009-MILUAV
TITLE: Test Verification
STATEMENT: Test verification includes test plan verification, test case verification, and test execution verification for military software testing.
RATIONALE: Test verification ensures testing quality and coverage.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 5. Validation activities

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SVVP-010-MILUAV
TITLE: Functional Validation
STATEMENT: Functional validation includes requirement validation, feature validation, and system behavior validation for military UAV operations.
RATIONALE: Functional validation ensures system functionality.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SVVP-011-MILUAV
TITLE: Performance Validation
STATEMENT: Performance validation includes real-time performance validation, throughput validation, and resource utilization validation for military systems.
RATIONALE: Performance validation ensures system performance.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SVVP-012-MILUAV
TITLE: Security Validation
STATEMENT: Security validation includes security requirement validation, threat analysis validation, and security testing validation for military systems.
RATIONALE: Security validation ensures system security.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SVVP-013-MILUAV
TITLE: Safety Validation
STATEMENT: Safety validation includes safety requirement validation, hazard analysis validation, and safety testing validation for military UAV operations.
RATIONALE: Safety validation ensures system safety.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 6. V&V criteria

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SVVP-014-MILUAV
TITLE: Acceptance Criteria
STATEMENT: Acceptance criteria include functional acceptance, performance acceptance, security acceptance, and safety acceptance criteria for military deployment.
RATIONALE: Acceptance criteria ensure system readiness.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SVVP-015-MILUAV
TITLE: Exit Criteria
STATEMENT: Exit criteria include verification exit criteria, validation exit criteria, and release exit criteria for military software development.
RATIONALE: Exit criteria ensure quality gates and milestones.

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: 7. Notes

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: SVVP-016-MILUAV
TITLE: V&V Documentation
STATEMENT: V&V documentation includes verification reports, validation reports, and compliance reports for military software development and deployment.
RATIONALE: V&V documentation ensures auditability and compliance.

[[/SECTION]] 